    {
      "id": "a1a14836ccd8e59cb45af554777164e1067a376f",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2775603786,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I do not believe that this is correct. The Server message in the Server Hello is exactly the same as the client. The Delegated Credential object itself \"MUST [be sent] as an extension in the CertificateEntry of its end-entity certificate,\" not in the Server or Client Hello. https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc9345#section-4.1.1\n\nHow was the capture file created?\n\nSee #20728",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-09-24T17:49:32.294Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-09-24T17:49:32.294Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 106517577,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 3528,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1edce3eabe4c01a46465766c609bc3091ca72575",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2775833155,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> How was the capture file created?\n\nEven if it was 4 years ago, I am pretty sure it was simple traffic generated using standard Firefox\n\nI think the current code only works with server authentication (RFC9341 4.1.1) but it fails with client auth (4.1.2) as reported in #20728 \n\nThe two different formats are not client_hello vs server_hello, but client_hello/cert_request vs certificate, IMO\n\nAn attempt to fix the issue: https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/merge_requests/21466",
          "author": {
            "id": 6875072,
            "username": "IvanNardi",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Ivan Nardi",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d4707801b74ca8478d56b09acecfa8671e536be3815713358ed72bab52474738?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/IvanNardi"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-09-24T19:51:58.389Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-09-24T20:05:41.528Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 106517577,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 3528,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    }
